TOTK: Ampere translation fixes for Vulkan, found on OoT's corpus (docs/oot-xlate.md):
* 1D fetches read row 0 of the one-row 2D texture, as Maxwell's (nxnative's (x & 0x3FFF, x >> 14) read is for a Metal
  host that binds texture buffers as 2D rows); IGpuAccessor.RecordTexelFetch1D goes again;
* TXQ: a component past the texture's dimensions reads 1 instead of an out-of-bounds OpCompositeExtract (74 shaders);
* StorageImageReadWithoutFormat declared for format-less storage images of Ampere jobs (56 compute shaders);
* ATOMG.CAS (0x3a9, field layout of Mesa NAK sm70_encode.rs OpAtom, MIT) and float add reductions (RED / ATOMG .F32.FTZ.RN)
  as compare-and-swap loops (34 shaders lost them);
* from MacNativeGames' patch 0006 (MIT, https://github.com/ly05010419/MacNativeGames @ 5843ee56f3ab6911e32d61d46e96fee4ce8137de), lost when patch 0019 took nxnative's files: F2FP.MERGE_C .H1 and CCTL
  (0x98f) as a no-op;
* patch 0017's goto elimination rule (no else that a goto may jump into) only for Ampere jobs, so a Maxwell translation
  keeps Ryujinx's structure (MacNativeGames measured 48 of TotK 1.4.3's 8,673 variants changing with it).

